{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <functional>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\n\nconst i64 MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint main() {\n    i64 p, k;\n    cin >> p >> k;\n    \n    vector<int> visited(p, 0);\n    \n    function<int(int)> dfs = [&](int x) -> int {\n        int cnt = 1;\n        visited[x] = 1;\n        while (!visited[(x * k) % p]) {\n            x = (x * k) % p;\n            visited[x] = 1;\n            cnt++;\n        }\n        return cnt;\n    };\n    \n    function<i64(i64, i64)> power = [&](i64 a, i64 b) -> i64 {\n        i64 res = 1;\n        while (b) {\n            if (b & 1) res = (res * a) % p;\n            b >>= 1;\n            a = (a * a) % p;\n        }\n        return res;\n    };\n    \n    i64 ans = 1;\n    \n    for (int i = 1; i < p; ++i) {\n        if (!visited[i]) {\n            i64 len = dfs(i);\n            i64 val = power(k, len);\n            if (val != 1 && val != 0) {\n                ans = (ans * (len + 1)) % MOD;\n            } else {\n                ans = (ans * p) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    if (k == 1) {\n        ans = (ans * p) % MOD;\n    }\n    \n    cout << ans << '\\n';\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    MOD = 1000000007\n    \n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    p = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    \n    visited = [0] * p\n    \n    def dfs(x):\n        cnt = 1\n        visited[x] = 1\n        while not visited[(x * k) % p]:\n            x = (x * k) % p\n            visited[x] = 1\n            cnt += 1\n        return cnt\n    \n    def power(a, b):\n        res = 1\n        while b:\n            if b & 1:\n                res = (res * a) % p\n            b >>= 1\n            a = (a * a) % p\n        return res\n    \n    ans = 1\n    \n    for i in range(1, p):\n        if not visited[i]:\n            length = dfs(i)\n            val = power(k, length)\n            if val != 1 and val != 0:\n                ans = (ans * (length + 1)) % MOD\n            else:\n                ans = (ans * p) % MOD\n    \n    if k == 1:\n        ans = (ans * p) % MOD\n    \n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00013290952483657748, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.30425164103507996, -7.998623186722398e-05, -0.023253949359059334, -0.8126696944236755, -0.0017049076268449426, -5.495397272170521e-05, -2.145764938177308e-06, -0.04287246614694595, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -5.960462772236497e-07, -9.643566590966657e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.5797485709190369, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.33824533224105835, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -0.10027053207159042, -9.65590606938349e-06, -0.05494064465165138, -4.410734163684538e-06, -5.411955